<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Details of Differential Privacy</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>DPM algorithm</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the private clustering algorithm, we use DPM from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liebenow et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. DPM recursively splits a dataset into clusters by identifying sparse regions while preserving differential privacy (DP). We allocate the privacy budget for the Gaussian mechanism with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\text{avg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>avg</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\text{avg}}</annotation></semantics></math> and for the exponential mechanism with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For ease of analysis, unlike the original paper, we assume that the size of the dataset and the size of the interval are <em id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">public</em>. By excluding them from the privacy budget, we can focus on protecting more sensitive aspects of the data while simplifying the analysis.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Privacy Accounting</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As privacy accounting involves composition, we utilize the following theorems for tight accounting.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Balle et al. (2018)</a></cite>)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Uniform</span> denotes sampling <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> elements from <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> data points without replacement
Let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\prime}=\mathcal{M}\circ\texttt{Uniform}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Uniform</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\prime}=\mathcal{M}\circ\texttt{Uniform}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathcal{M}^{\prime}}(\varepsilon^{\prime})\leq(m/n)\delta_{\mathcal{M}}(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathcal{M}^{\prime}}(\varepsilon^{\prime})\leq(m/n)\delta_{\mathcal{M}}(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{\prime}=\log(1+(m/n)(e^{\varepsilon}-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{\prime}=\log(1+(m/n)(e^{\varepsilon}-1))</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (DP to RDP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bun and Steinke (2016)</a></cite>)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The exponential mechanism is <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-DP and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,\varepsilon_{\texttt{EM}}(\alpha))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">EM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,\varepsilon_{\texttt{EM}}(\alpha))</annotation></semantics></math>-RDP, where <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\texttt{EM}}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">EM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\texttt{EM}}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="A1.Ex2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:18.9pt;vertical-align:-4.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(75.4pt,-4.1pt) scale(1.77639318312007,1.77639318312007) ;">
<p id="A1.Ex2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min\left(\frac{\alpha}{2}\varepsilon^{2},\frac{1}{\alpha-1}\log\left(\frac{\sinh(\alpha\varepsilon)-\sinh((\alpha-1)\varepsilon)}{\sinh(\varepsilon)}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>sinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>sinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>sinh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min\left(\frac{\alpha}{2}\varepsilon^{2},\frac{1}{\alpha-1}\log\left(\frac{\sinh(\alpha\varepsilon)-\sinh((\alpha-1)\varepsilon)}{\sinh(\varepsilon)}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (RDP composition)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If each mechanism <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{M}_{i})_{i=1}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{M}_{i})_{i=1}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-RDP, then the composition <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}\circ A_{k-1}\circ\dots\circ A_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}\circ A_{k-1}\circ\dots\circ A_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,k\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,k\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>-RDP.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (RDP to approximate DP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Balle et al. (2019)</a></cite>)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If a mechanism <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,\rho)</annotation></semantics></math>-RDP then it is <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\rho+\log((\alpha-1)/\alpha)-(\log\delta+\log\alpha)/(\alpha-1),\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\rho+\log((\alpha-1)/\alpha)-(\log\delta+\log\alpha)/(\alpha-1),\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>-DP for any <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">When accounting exponential mechanism of DPM, we first apply theorem <a href="#A1.Ex2" title="Theorem 2 (DP to RDP ( ) ) ‣ A.2 Privacy Accounting ‣ Appendix A Details of Differential Privacy ‣ Public Data Assisted Differentially Private In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Then the calculate privacy loss of composition by calling <span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">compose_subsampled_EM</span> API using <span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">AutoDP</span> package. Then, the converting RDP to approx DP using theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (RDP to approximate DP ( ) ) ‣ A.2 Privacy Accounting ‣ Appendix A Details of Differential Privacy ‣ Public Data Assisted Differentially Private In-Context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. For the Gaussian mechanism of DPM, we use <span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DPSGDAccount</span> from the <span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">prv_accountant</span> library.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> <span id="alg2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DPM</span>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liebenow et al., 2024</a>)</cite></figcaption>
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D,\tau_{r},R,t,q,\alpha,\varepsilon_{\text{int}},\varepsilon_{\text{cnt}},\varepsilon_{\text{exp}},\varepsilon_{\text{avg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>int</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>cnt</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>avg</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D,\tau_{r},R,t,q,\alpha,\varepsilon_{\text{int}},\varepsilon_{\text{cnt}},\varepsilon_{\text{exp}},\varepsilon_{\text{avg}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            clusters <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            weights <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\varepsilon_{\text{cnt},i}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}}=\left(\varepsilon_{\text{cnt}}\frac{\sqrt{2^{i}}}{\sum_{j=0}^{\tau_{r}}\sqrt{2^{j}}}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mtext>cnt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>cnt</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msqrt><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msup></msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><msqrt><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\varepsilon_{\text{cnt},i}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}}=\left(\varepsilon_{\text{cnt}}\frac{\sqrt{2^{i}}}{\sum_{j=0}^{\tau_{r}}\sqrt{2^{j}}}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\varepsilon_{\text{exp},i}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}-1}=\left(\varepsilon_{\text{exp}}\frac{\sqrt{2^{i}}}{\sum_{j=0}^{\tau_{r}-1}\sqrt{2^{j}}}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mtext>exp</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msqrt><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></msup></msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msqrt><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>j</mi></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\varepsilon_{\text{exp},i}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}-1}=\left(\varepsilon_{\text{exp}}\frac{\sqrt{2^{i}}}{\sum_{j=0}^{\tau_{r}-1}\sqrt{2^{j}}}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}-1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left(\lambda_{i}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}}=\left(-\ln(2\delta)/\varepsilon_{\text{cnt},i}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mtext>cnt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\lambda_{i}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}}=\left(-\ln(2\delta)/\varepsilon_{\text{cnt},i}\right)_{i=0}^{\tau_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">// Dataset size perturbation</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{n}=|D|+\text{Lap}(\varepsilon_{\text{cnt},0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Lap</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mtext>cnt</mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{n}=|D|+\text{Lap}(\varepsilon_{\text{cnt},0})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">// Private interval size estimation</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\text{IntervalSizeEst}(D,\tilde{n},\varepsilon_{\text{int}},\text{sigmas})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>IntervalSizeEst</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>int</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><mtext>sigmas</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\text{IntervalSizeEst}(D,\tilde{n},\varepsilon_{\text{int}},\text{sigmas})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{numSplits}=(b-a)/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>numSplits</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{numSplits}=(b-a)/\beta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BuildClustering</span>(<math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D,\tilde{n},0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D,\tilde{n},0</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">// Privately compute the cluster 
<br class="ltx_break">centers</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\{\text{DPAvg}(C_{i},\tilde{n},\varepsilon_{\text{avg}})\mid C_{i}\in\text{clusters}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>DPAvg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mtext>avg</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mtext>clusters</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{\text{DPAvg}(C_{i},\tilde{n},\varepsilon_{\text{avg}})\mid C_{i}\in\text{clusters}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C,\text{weights}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>weights</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C,\text{weights}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">procedure</span> <span id="alg2.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">BuildClustering</span>(<math id="alg2.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S,\tilde{n},y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S,\tilde{n},y</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg2.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\geq\tau_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\geq\tau_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
              
              
               halt and add <math id="alg2.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to clusters and <math id="alg2.l18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{n}</annotation></semantics></math> to weights

</div>
<div id="alg2.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
              
              
